      "rev_n_1_e7582e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_e7582e_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_e7582e",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through each package size from 1 to k and calculate the minimum number of packages needed for each size. Choose the size that requires the fewest packages.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794389911.9501
      },
      "rev_n_2_ac3e9e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_ac3e9e_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_ac3e9e",
        "thought_text": "Directly compute the minimum number of packages needed by dividing n by each possible package size i (from 1 to k) and taking the ceiling of the division result. Track the minimum across all possibilities.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794389911.9501078
      },
      "rev_n_3_4d30a1_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_4d30a1_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_4d30a1",
        "thought_text": "Use mathematical insight to recognize that the optimal package size is the greatest common divisor (GCD) of n and any number from 1 to k. Calculate the minimum number of packages needed using this insight.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794389911.950112
      },
      "rev_n_4_d22cb0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_d22cb0_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_d22cb0",
        "thought_text": "Re-evaluate the use of GCD. The current approach calculates the GCD between n and k, but it might be more effective to consider the GCD between n and each possible package size from 1 to k, as the problem requires buying packages of the same size.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5016640051165702801",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794389966.89613
      },
      "rev_n_5_a52012_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_a52012_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_a52012",
        "thought_text": "Consider edge cases where n is less than k. In such cases, the optimal solution might involve buying packages of size 1, as buying larger packages would exceed the required number of shovels.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5016640051165702801",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794389966.896142
      },
      "rev_n_6_9186a7_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_9186a7_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_9186a7",
        "thought_text": "Implement a brute-force approach by iterating through each possible package size from 1 to k and calculating the number of packages needed for each size. Keep track of the minimum number of packages required across all sizes.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5016640051165702801",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794389966.896147
      },
      "rev_n_7_aadb99_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_aadb99_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_aadb99",
        "thought_text": "Directly compute the minimum number of packages needed by dividing n by each possible package size i (from 1 to k) and taking the ceiling of the division result. Track the minimum across all possibilities.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1598375835713105084",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794389995.8623989
      },
      "rev_n_8_a51530_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_a51530_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_a51530",
        "thought_text": "Instead of iterating through all possible package sizes, start checking from the largest possible package size (min(n, k)) down to 1. This reduces the number of iterations significantly because larger packages will result in fewer packages needed.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1598375835713105084",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794389995.862432
      },
      "rev_n_9_5a3ed1_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_5a3ed1_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_5a3ed1",
        "thought_text": "Precompute the results for a range of n and k values and use these precomputed results to answer queries. This can be done using dynamic programming or memoization to avoid redundant calculations.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1598375835713105084",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794389995.86245
      },
      "rev_n_10_9f624f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_9f624f_0",
        "node_id": "n_10_9f624f",
        "thought_text": "Re-evaluate the logic for calculating the minimum number of packages. The current approach might not correctly handle all edge cases, especially when n is much larger than k.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1402072538258100716",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
